{"id":"n-20261010-6ztl2k","category":"health","display_title":"Expert Coaching Strategies for Better Running","display_title_he":"אסטרטגיות אימון מומחיות לריצה טובה יותר","short_summary":"Top athletic coaches share practical guidance on building long-term running habits, avoiding injuries, selecting proper gear, and mastering nutrition. By prioritizing strength, consistency, and comfortable pace over high-tech gadgets, runners of all levels can achieve sustainable progress.","english_level":"C1","words":509,"reading_time":4,"image":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/IGEN_ENVIRONTHON_2024_%28_in_aligned_to_UN_COP29_%E2%80%93_UN_Climate_Change_Conference_2024%29.png/960px-IGEN_ENVIRONTHON_2024_%28_in_aligned_to_UN_COP29_%E2%80%93_UN_Climate_Change_Conference_2024%29.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","credit":"IGEN ENVIROTHON · CC0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IGEN_ENVIRONTHON_2024_(_in_aligned_to_UN_COP29_%E2%80%93_UN_Climate_Change_Conference_2024).png"},"sources":[{"name":"The Guardian","domain":"theguardian.com","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2026/oct/10/strength-stretches-expert-tips-to-make-you-a-better-runner","title":"Expert tips to make you a better runner - start slow, enlist a friend, choose strength over stretches","published_at":"2026-10-10T04:00:47.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-10T04:00:47.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-10T06:15:42.888Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["Taking up running is widely heralded as one of the most accessible ways to enhance physical fitness, yet maintaining long-term momentum and avoiding injury present formidable challenges for beginners and experienced runners alike. According to veteran coaches, overcoming the initial psychological barrier is frequently the most difficult step. Thomas Craggs, who leads the World Class Endurance Programme for UK Athletics, points out that even elite marathon runners experience days when personal motivation wanes, making disciplined routine far more vital than fleeting inspiration. Beginners are strongly advised to embrace initial discomfort, as rapid cardiovascular progression typically occurs within just a few weeks. Digital tools such as the Couch to 5K application provide structured walk-run intervals, encouraging novices to maintain a gentle, conversational pace rather than sprinting prematurely. Running experts emphasize that incorporating frequent walking breaks is not a failure, but rather a strategic method to build baseline endurance safely.","When selecting footwear and training attire, expert consensus strongly favours personal comfort over high-tech performance features. Allie Bailey, an ultrarunner and coaching author, advises recreational runners against overinvesting in expensive, highly specialized equipment. While carbon-plated running shoes offer measurable performance gains for competitive athletes, coaches warn that their relative lack of lateral stability can precipitate lower-limb injuries if worn during routine training sessions. Instead, prospective runners should seek impartial gait analysis at independent retail shops to identify shoes tailored to their specific biomechanics. Furthermore, high-performance athletic apparel is entirely unnecessary at the outset; functional secondhand clothing provides an accessible, environmentally sustainable alternative that eliminates financial barriers to entry before heading out the door.","To sustain long-term progress without suffering physical burnout, establishing clear personal targets is essential. Participating in organized community events like parkrun offers structured motivation within an inclusive environment where walking is actively encouraged alongside running. Coach Craggs recommends a foundational frequency of three runs per week, striking an optimal balance between physical stimulus and adequate physiological recovery time. When athletic gains inevitably plateau, introducing controlled high-intensity interval workouts can safely challenge the cardiovascular system beyond its habitual comfort zone. Crucially, experts caution against becoming excessively reliant on modern smartwatches and fitness trackers. While digital wearables deliver valuable metrics, allowing real-time data to dictate emotional state or trigger overexertion can undermine the crucial skill of natural pace judgment.","Proper nutritional management and targeted strength conditioning play equally critical roles in preventing injury and supporting athletic development. Pre-workout dietary preparation should prioritize easily digestible carbohydrates such as bananas, porridge, or honeyed toast, while conventional cow's milk serves as an economical, highly effective post-run recovery drink due to its balanced combination of protein and carbohydrates. Regarding flexibility, brief token stretches offer minimal physiological benefit; instead, coaches advocate for regular yoga practice or targeted unilateral strength exercises—such as split squats, lunges, single-leg calf raises, and low-level plyometric hops. Building structural strength preserves muscle mass and bone density, particularly as runners age, helping them remain injury-free. Finally, coaches stress that runners must never attempt to push through sharp pain, as continuing to train on an unaddressed injury will inevitably exacerbate physical damage."],"facts":[{"fact":"Thomas Craggs, head of the World Class Endurance Programme for UK Athletics, emphasizes that even elite runners experience dips in motivation and must rely on routine.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Beginners can see rapid progression from running for short intervals to continuous running within weeks.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Apps like Couch to 5K and walking intervals help build endurance while reducing injury risks.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Experts recommend comfortable shoes and gait analysis over expensive carbon-plated performance shoes, which lack lateral stability.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Community events such as parkrun encourage all fitness levels and permit walking.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Training three times a week balances physical stimulus with adequate physiological recovery time.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Interval training helps runners overcome performance plateaus.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Relying too heavily on smartwatch data can increase anxiety and disrupt natural pace judgment.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Pre-workout carbohydrates like porridge, bananas, or toast provide fuel, while cow's milk serves as a cheap and effective post-run recovery drink.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Targeted unilateral strength training (lunges, split squats, single-leg calf raises) is more effective for runners than brief stretching routines.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Strength training helps preserve muscle mass and bone density, particularly as runners age.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Runners should never attempt to run through pain and should consult a physiotherapist or osteopath if daily life is affected.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"taking up","lemma":"take up","pos":"phrasal verb","he":"להתחיל לעסוק ב-","name":false},{"text":"running","lemma":"running","pos":"noun","he":"ריצה","name":false},{"text":"widely","lemma":"widely","pos":"adverb","he":"ברחבי תבל / באופן נרחב","name":false},{"text":"heralded","lemma":"herald","pos":"verb","he":"משובח / מוקלס / מואדר","name":false},{"text":"accessible","lemma":"accessible","pos":"adjective","he":"נגיש","name":false},{"text":"enhance","lemma":"enhance","pos":"verb","he":"לשפר / לשדרג","name":false},{"text":"physical fitness","lemma":"physical fitness","pos":"noun","he":"כושר גופני","name":false},{"text":"maintaining","lemma":"maintain","pos":"verb","he":"לשמור על / לתחזק","name":false},{"text":"long-term","lemma":"long-term","pos":"adjective","he":"טווח ארוך","name":false},{"text":"momentum","lemma":"momentum","pos":"noun","he":"מומנטום / תנופה","name":false},{"text":"avoiding","lemma":"avoid","pos":"verb","he":"להימנע מ-","name":false},{"text":"injury","lemma":"injury","pos":"noun","he":"פציעה","name":false},{"text":"present","lemma":"present","pos":"verb","he":"ציב / מעורר","name":false},{"text":"formidable","lemma":"formidable","pos":"adjective","he":"מרשים / מאתגר מאוד","name":false},{"text":"challenges","lemma":"challenge","pos":"noun","he":"אתגרים","name":false},{"text":"beginners","lemma":"beginner","pos":"noun","he":"מתחילים","name":false},{"text":"experienced","lemma":"experienced","pos":"adjective","he":"מנוסים","name":false},{"text":"alike","lemma":"alike","pos":"adverb","he":"כאחד / במידה שווה","name":false},{"text":"according to","lemma":"according to","pos":"preposition","he":"לפי / על פי","name":false},{"text":"veteran","lemma":"veteran","pos":"adjective","he":"וותיק","name":false},{"text":"coaches","lemma":"coach","pos":"noun","he":"מאמנים","name":false},{"text":"overcoming","lemma":"overcome","pos":"verb","he":" להתגבר על","name":false},{"text":"initial","lemma":"initial","pos":"adjective","he":"ראשוני","name":false},{"text":"psychological","lemma":"psychological","pos":"adjective","he":"פסיכולוגי","name":false},{"text":"barrier","lemma":"barrier","pos":"noun","he":"מחסום","name":false},{"text":"frequently","lemma":"frequently","pos":"adverb","he":"לעיתים קרובות","name":false},{"text":"difficult","lemma":"difficult","pos":"adjective","he":"קשה","name":false},{"text":"step","lemma":"step","pos":"noun","he":"צעד / שלב","name":false},{"text":"Thomas Craggs","lemma":"Thomas Craggs","pos":"name","he":"תומאס קראגס","name":true},{"text":"leads","lemma":"lead","pos":"verb","he":"מוביל / מנהל","name":false},{"text":"World Class Endurance Programme","lemma":"World Class Endurance Programme","pos":"name","he":"תכנית הסיבולת הבינלאומית","name":true},{"text":"UK Athletics","lemma":"UK Athletics","pos":"name","he":"איגוד